cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use prd-grill, the Grill -> Gate -> Build pattern, or the prd-gate
  independent spec gate in your work, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "prd-grill: Grill -> Gate -> Build — interrogate requirements, score them with an independent gate, then hand the human-approved PRD to autonomous development"
authors:
  - family-names: Gao
    given-names: Sam
    alias: samgao2000
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-06-11
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/samgao2000/prd-grill
url: https://github.com/samgao2000/prd-grill
keywords:
  - requirements engineering
  - PRD
  - LLM-as-judge
  - quality gate
  - agentic coding
  - agent skills
abstract: >-
  Three agent skills for agentic software delivery. req-dev-lite interrogates
  the requirements provider until requirements are falsifiable (Mom Test,
  Impact Mapping, 5 Whys, Specification by Example, Cockburn Extensions,
  INVEST, Volere Quality Gateway). prd-gate scores the resulting PRD on 11
  dimensions with a deterministic layer plus a fresh-context LLM judge that
  never sees the elicitation conversation, and emits a machine-readable
  verdict and requirement_confidence. auto-dev-lite builds from the gated PRD
  AFK and refuses a FAIL or unscored spec. The integration with ECC adds the
  judge as an agent and a hook that blocks planning from ungated PRDs.
